answer:
l. who have signed the DSU for benefits under the right to education after the deadline for submitting a scholarship application; m. for whom it has not been possible to obtain ISEE data within the time limits laid down in Article 11(8) of Prime Ministerial Decree 159/2013, and in particular applications that refer to certificates/DSUs:

• Not found in the INPS database; • Do not include the ISEE for university education grants and/or do not relate to the student applying for the benefits; • Not yet calculated for the purposes of determining ISEE values (certificate); n. who have submitted their application after the deadline set out in this call for applications;

o. who are either behind in their studies or repeating a year; p. foreign nationals who do not hold a residence permit for the academic year 2026/2027; q. students enrolled on the open semester referred to in Legislative Decree No. After the deadline for applying for benefits: • Students can change their IBAN by accessing the ‘Student Portal’ screen. • Any other event occurring after the application for benefits has been submitted must be reported to ERDIS without delay by opening a ticket, and will be subject to assessment. A student who has submitted a request for an ISEE calculation for university benefits by the deadline for scholarship applications, but has been excluded from the provisional ranking due to the failure to produce said data within the time limits set out in Article 11, paragraph 8 of Prime Ministerial Decree 159/2013, may lodge an appeal to request a review of their position.
